@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "POPIA privacy notice";
}

<article class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language notice</p>
    <h1>POPIA privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="lead text-muted">This explains what eProcure collects and why. It is not legal advice.</p>
</article>

<div class="surface-card mb-3">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>For user accounts, we collect your full name, email address, optional phone number, password hash and account role. For supplier profiles, we collect optional job title and contact number plus the date you accepted this notice.</p>
    <p>For supplier companies, we collect the legal name, CIPC registration number, SARS tax compliance PIN, CSD number, B-BBEE level and sector. Tender applications include SBD declarations, payment references and documents you choose to upload.</p>
    <p>For accountability, we record the acting user, email, IP address, action and UTC timestamp in the audit log. We never collect card numbers, bank details, ID numbers, home addresses or dates of birth in this MVP.</p>
</div>
<div class="surface-card mb-3">
    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use this information to authenticate users, protect tenant access, check tender eligibility, receive and evaluate applications, process a tender fee through the selected provider, communicate about an application and preserve an accountable procurement record.</p>
</div>
<div class="surface-card mb-3">
    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>You can see your own account, company, applications and documents. The organisation that owns a tender can see a supplier's company, application, documents and contact details only after the application becomes visible under the payment rules. Other organisations and suppliers cannot see them.</p>
</div>
<div class="surface-card mb-3">
    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>Procurement, payment and audit records are retained for the applicable public-sector records-management period. Documents are stored outside the public web folder and are served only after an ownership or tenant check. You may contact the platform operator to ask about access, correction or retention of your information.</p>
</div>
<div class="surface-card">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p class="mb-0">For a privacy question, contact the eProcure platform operator through the programme contact channel supplied by your organisation.</p>
</div>